/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123709101,imgsize-748073.cms"/></item><item><title>‘Alligator Alcatraz’ case: US court allows Florida detention centre to run; reverses order</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123709020.cms" /&gt;</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/alligator-alcatraz-case-us-court-allows-florida-detention-centre-to-run-reverses-order/articleshow/123709020.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/alligator-alcatraz-case-us-court-allows-florida-detention-centre-to-run-reverses-order/articleshow/123709020.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-05T05:38:16+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123709082,imgsize-255738.cms"/></item><item><title>US to block visas for Central Americans aiding China; Rubio issues warning</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123708935.cms" /&gt;The US will restrict visas for Central Americans working for the CCP to undermine the rule of law in their countries. Secretary of State Marco Rubio announced the policy, targeting individuals who knowingly support CCP activities that destabilize legal and political systems. This action reflects the US commitment to countering China's influence and protecting American interests in Central America.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/wont-allow-regional-destabilisation-us-to-block-visas-for-central-americans-aiding-china-rubio-issues-warning/articleshow/123708935.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/wont-allow-regional-destabilisation-us-to-block-visas-for-central-americans-aiding-china-rubio-issues-warning/articleshow/123708935.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-05T05:13:50+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123708995,imgsize-28666.cms"/></item><item><title>Chinese cyberattackers may've stolen data from almost every American</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123708878.cms" /&gt;A sweeping cyberattack, dubbed Salt Typhoon and attributed to China, has targeted over 80 countries, potentially compromising data from nearly every American. This years-long, coordinated assault infiltrated major telecommunications firms, raising concerns about China's growing cyber capabilities and ambitions for global influence.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/chinese-cyberattackers-mayve-stolen-data-from-almost-every-american/articleshow/123708878.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/chinese-cyberattackers-mayve-stolen-data-from-almost-every-american/articleshow/123708878.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-05T04:35:41+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-123708881,imgsize-103298.cms"/></item><item><title>Armani's passes away: Who will inherit the billion-dollar fashion empire?</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/123706552.cms" /&gt;</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/giorgio-armanis-passes-away-who-will-inherit-the-billion-dollar-fashion-empire-family-collaborators-and-whats-next/articleshow/123706552.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/giorgio-armanis-passes-away-who-will-inherit-the-billion-dollar-fashion-empire-family-collaborators-and-whats-next/articleshow/123706552.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-05